[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch_dist_1_1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the Layer-3 control plane (FRRouting/OSPF) on the distribution switch for pod 1 (switch_dist_1_1).

Mechanism: host_1_1_1_1 forwards off-subnet traffic to its default gateway 10.1.1.1 (br0 on switch_dist_1_1). That gateway has no routes to external networks, so it immediately returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable.” This matches the user symptom of being unable to reach anything outside the subnet.

Localization evidence:
- From host_1_1_1_1, ping to 10.200.0.3 fails with “From 10.1.1.1 Destination Net Unreachable,” while ARP/ICMP to the gateway succeeds (ARP entry for 10.1.1.1 present; ping to 10.1.1.1 OK).
- On switch_dist_1_1, the routing table contains only connected routes (10.1.1.0/24 on br0 and 172.16.0.6/31 on eth0) and cannot ping 10.200.0.3.
- FRR/OSPF is down: “frr.service: inactive (dead)” and “ospfd is not running.”
- Contrast: switch_dist_2_1 has OSPF up and has learned routes to 10.200.0.0/24, and host_2_1_1_1 reaches the server farm successfully.

Root cause: FRR/OSPF is not running (and no active OSPF configuration is present) on switch_dist_1_1, leaving it with only connected routes.

Corrective fix: Do not replace the access switch. On switch_dist_1_1, start/enable FRR and configure OSPF to the core (eth0 in area 0.0.0.1) and advertise 10.1.1.0/24 (passive on br0). After OSPF adjacency forms, external routes (e.g., 10.200.0.0/24) will be learned and host_1_1_1_1 will regain reachability. Hardware swap not required. 
=== END ===